        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $n\\ge2$ and let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^n$ be a nonempty bounded connected open set whose boundary is covered by finitely many $C^1$ graph charts. Give $H^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)=W^{1,2}(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ its Sobolev norm, let $H_0^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ be the $H^1$-closure of $C_c^\\infty(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$, and let $W^{1/2,2}(\\partial\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ have the finite-chart Slobodeckij norm. Define $\\mathcal D(\\Omega):=H^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)/H_0^1(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ with its quotient norm. The trace induces a bounded linear bijection $\\overline T:\\mathcal D(\\Omega)\\to W^{1/2,2}(\\partial\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ with bounded inverse, so these two norms are equivalent under the induced identification. The induced map after quotienting by constants is also a bounded linear bijection $\\mathcal D(\\Omega)/\\mathbb K\\mathbf1\\to W^{1/2,2}(\\partial\\Omega;\\mathbb K)/\\mathbb K$, with equivalent quotient norms. A continuous linear functional on $W^{1/2,2}(\\partial\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ descends to the constant quotient exactly when it annihilates constants, and its descended functional has the quotient dual norm."
